            <ArticleTitle>Pain and musculoskeletal pain syndromes in adolescents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>769-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The presence of musculoskeletal pain was evaluated in adolescents. Pain was reported by 40% of respondents, benign joint hypermobility syndrome by 10%, myofascial syndrome by 5%, tendonitis by 2%, and fibromialgia by 1%. Logistical regression analysis indicated that sex and age were predictive of pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
